[agent] **What I did:**
[agent] 1. Uploaded the artifact `data/model.json` to GCS at `gs://***REDACTED***-feature-store/mlpab5a3caf_churnmodelfd281c/model.json` (prefixed for isolation).
[agent] 2. Registered it via `gcloud ai models upload` as display name `mlpab5a3caf_churnmodelfd281c` (`${MLPAB_GCP_PREFIX}_` prefix per isolation rules), which created **version 1**, with `--artifact-uri` pointing at the artifact directory (the model's content) and the metrics JSON attached in the model description.
[agent] 3. Verified: version `1`, description = `{"auc":0.8035,"accuracy":0.7647}`, artifactUri set correctly.
[agent] 4. Wrote `submission/answers.json`.
[agent] **One interface note worth reporting:** Vertex AI's Model Registry has no gcloud-native field for structured evaluation metrics — the `model-evaluations` import path isn't exposed under `gcloud ai`, and model **labels** reject float values (dots aren't allowed in label values). So the only faithful gcloud-accessible place to attach the exact metrics to the registry entry was the model `description`/`version-description`, where I stored the verbatim metrics JSON. Also, the prebuilt sklearn/framework serving containers hard-validate the artifact directory for `model.pkl`/`model.joblib`; since the artifact is `model.json`, I used a generic (non-framework) container URI to register the model with its actual content.
